#: rc.cpp:89
msgid "Support Quanta With Financial Donation"
msgstr ""

#: rc.cpp:91
msgid ""
"<div align=\"center\">"
"<h2>Your contribution can make a "
"difference</h2></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Quanta Plus is one of the few "
"programs in KDE that benefits from a full time developer, Andras Mantia. Our "
"development has been largely\n"
"sponsored by the efforts of the Project Manager, Eric Laffoon. In addition "
"to his minimum 10-20 hour a week time commitment, his\n"
"company, <a href=\"http://kittyhooch.com\" target=\"_blank\">Kitty Hooch</a>"
" LLP has an ongoing financial commitment to Quanta\n"
"development. This financial support has proven to be <i>crucial</i> to "
"keeping\n"
"Quanta in continuous development. It is also a catalyst to our volunteer\n"
"developers."
"<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Kitty Hooch is a small company with no "
"employees, 2 active partners and several\n"
"contract workers. After test marketing in the fall of 2001 they began "
"wholesale and retail to national and international destinations in early "
"2002. Kitty Hooch controls all aspects of\n"
"their product production and marketing. Kitty Hooch must preserve a portion "
"of it's revenue for essential investment capital to sustain and to grow. "
"Quanta sponsorship is no small expense. Maintaining the dream of Quanta was "
"unfortunately more costly than imagined in 2003. Fortunately two other "
"individuals have stepped up to $200 and $100 a month commitments "
"respectively. This, along with your donations, has empowered us to continue. "
"During this time our Eric has been improving his C++ skills with the hope of "
"putting in more time coding. Financial concerns can take time, focus and "
"joy.<div\n"
"align=\"center\"><h3>Balancing open source ideals and fiscal\n"
"reality</h3></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;We believe that the open source "
"model\n"
"is the future of software, but it is no guarantee of success. How many open\n"
"source projects that we had high hopes for are unmaintained today? In early "
"2002 many people thought that\n"
"Quanta Plus was dead. Developing a best in class tool is no easy task. We "
"believe the key is consistent momentum. Nothing insures\n"
"this better than programmers who can work without financial or time "
"distractions. Why do\n"
"you think OSS projects die?<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;As Quanta grows\n"
"the project management demands are increasing and ironically impacting the\n"
"revenue stream it requires to continue. The impact of the coding efforts of\n"
"Andras, our full time lead developer, has been huge! We\n"
"are looking to make Quanta grow even faster. We want to get Eric more "
"involved in coding and less involved trying to balance getting his business "
"to where it should be with finding money for Andras. We would like to have "
"an opportunity to Fly Andras to the US to meet with Eric and discuss Quanta "
"more productively than over email. <i>We\n"
"want to make Quanta the best web tool anywhere!</i>. This will require a "
"nucleus or active core developers.\n"
"We're hoping professional developers and companies using Quanta will help us "
"to reach our goals with sponsorship donations that will relieve financial "
"stresses.<div\n"
"align=\"center\"><h3>Could Quanta die without your\n"
"support?</h3></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;No! But from February 2001 to "
"June\n"
"2002 there was very little activity and many months with no work done at "
"all.\n"
"Andras first coded for the project in December of 2001. He was sponsored "
"and\n"
"went full time mid 2002. What if we had we not lost those months? We "
"estimate\n"
"that small contributions from less than 0.05% - 0.1% of Quanta users would "
"easily\n"
"sponsor two full time developers and help volunteers with needs critical to\n"
"their development efforts. Possibly this would even support branching to "
"other open source projects of benefit to our users. We value and pursue "
"volunteer developers, but full time developers are\n"
"many times as productive! We're asking you to help us grow the project and\n"
"continue to fulfil your requests.<br><div align=\"center\"><h3>Will you\n"
"help?</h3></div>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you wish to donate through "
"PayPal\n"
"(online money transfer or credit card), visit our <a\n"
"href=\"http://quanta.sourceforge.net/main1.php?actfile=donate\">donation\n"
"page</a>. "
"<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;If you are outside the PayPal area or wish\n"
"to discuss corporate sponsorship contact the project\n"
"manager:<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Eric Laffoon, <a\n"
"href=\"mailto:sequitur@kde.org?subject=Quanta%20sponsorship%20inquiry\">"
"sequitur@kde.org</a>"
msgstr ""

